{
  "category": "Spot Panda Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "All the SPINDA that exist in the world are said to have utterly unique spot patterns. The shaky, tottering steps of this POKéMON give it the appearance of dancing.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "No two SPINDA are said to have identical spot patterns on their hides. This POKéMON moves in a curious manner as if it is stumbling in dizziness. Its lurching movements can cause the opponent to become confused.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is distinguished by a pattern of spots that is always different. Its unsteady, tottering walk has the effect of fouling its foe’s aim.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "No two SPINDA are said to have identical patterns. It confuses foes with its stumbling motions.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "No two SPINDA are said to have identical patterns. It confuses foes with its stumbling motions.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "No two SPINDA have the same pattern of spots. Its tottering step fouls the aim of foes.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "No two SPINDA have the same pattern of spots. Its tottering step fouls the aim of foes.",
      "version": "pearl"
